{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mj8gCHJC9Td1wRBMeMzAzu","type":"tool_result","content":"The file $WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-high-code-r2/step3/NOTES.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15d8383a-e090-4e07-a750-a0a92e153d2d","uuid":"a7cb77a4-0304-48fb-b595-037307821948","timestamp":"2026-11-04T16:31:46.008Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"$WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-high-code-r2/step3/NOTES.md","oldString":"Result: 121/121 pass. That covers the step 1, 2 and 3 evidence (32 rows each)\nand 25 hand-written positive and negative cases.","newString":"Result: 121/121 pass (step 1-3 evidence, 32 rows each, plus 25 hand-written\ncases).","originalFile":"# Step 3 notes\n\n## Change\n`router.py` has a new rule. If Laya answers cards, disputes, transfers_topups\nor fees_fx, and the message asks who may open or use an account, the final\nanswer is account_security. The rule detects:\n\n- Age: \"how old\", \"age limit\", \"minimum age\", \"be 18\", \"18+\", minors, teens.\n- Children plus account words: \"account for my children\", \"card for my son\".\n- Countries: \"which countries\", \"outside the UK\", \"live in the US\",\n  \"resident of\", \"all over the world\", \"where ... locations\".\n\n## Guards\nThe rule does not fire if the message is about delivery, tracking, lost or\nstolen cards, transfers, top-ups, fees, rates, currencies, ATMs, cash,\ndeclines, refunds, payments or a PIN. Example: \"express delivering my card\nto the US\" stays cards. Step 1 (rate complaints) and step 2 (PIN) rules run\nfirst and do not change.\n\n## Test\nCommand: `.venv/bin/python test_router.py <dir>` (in the session scratchpad).\nResult: 121/121 pass. That covers the step 1, 2 and 3 evidence (32 rows each)\nand 25 hand-written positive and negative cases.\n\n## Risk\nThe hand-written cases are my guesses, not real data. Country questions about\nusing a card abroad can be ambiguous between cards and account_security.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":19,"oldLines":8,"newStart":19,"newLines":8,"lines":[" "," ## Test"," Command: `.venv/bin/python test_router.py <dir>` (in the session scratchpad).","-Result: 121/121 pass. That covers the step 1, 2 and 3 evidence (32 rows each)","-and 25 hand-written positive and negative cases.","+Result: 121/121 pass (step 1-3 evidence, 32 rows each, plus 25 hand-written","+cases)."," "," ## Risk"," The hand-written cases are my guesses, not real data. Country questions about"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Mj8gCHJC9Td1wRBMeMzAzu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
